 "pg_test_fsync_raw": "5 seconds per test\nO_DIRECT supported on this platform for open_datasync and open_sync.\n\nCompare file sync methods using one 8kB write:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      3713.852 ops/sec     269 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          3563.580 ops/sec     281 usecs/op\n        fsync                              3702.763 ops/sec     270 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          3711.404 ops/sec     269 usecs/op\n\nCompare file sync methods using two 8kB writes:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      3494.130 ops/sec     286 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          3597.031 ops/sec     278 usecs/op\n        fsync                              3572.966 ops/sec     280 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          3473.972 ops/sec     288 usecs/op\n\nCompare open_sync with different write sizes:\n(This is designed to compare the cost of writing 16kB in different write\nopen_sync sizes.)\n         1 * 16kB open_sync write          4876.628 ops/sec     205 usecs/op\n         2 *  8kB open_sync writes         4784.980 ops/sec     209 usecs/op\n         4 *  4kB open_sync writes         3294.100 ops/sec     304 usecs/op\n         8 *  2kB open_sync writes          148.998 ops/sec    6711 usecs/op\n        16 *  1kB open_sync writes           47.985 ops/sec   20840 usecs/op\n\nTest if fsync on non-write file descriptor is honored:\n(If the times are similar, fsync() can sync data written on a different\ndescriptor.)\n        write, fsync, close                5120.900 ops/sec     195 usecs/op\n        write, close, fsync                5066.343 ops/sec     197 usecs/op\n\nNon-sync'ed 8kB writes:\n        write                           1911251.942 ops/sec       1 usecs/op\n",
